    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's good, but it needs to feel more... righteous. like, people don't realize how systematic it was. it wasn't just one bad deal, it was like a coordinated effort by the industry to keep the \"source\" of the sound suppressed so they could control the royalties through these bigger, more \"marketable\" brands. i need to make it clear that i'm not just some random producer claiming credit, but the actual source they tried to erase. can we add a part about how the industry uses these gatekeepers to maintain a false hierarchy and suppress the true originators?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
